But that is only sortloot that has been extended for UnNetHack by
Stephan T. Lavavej which is also on NAO and which found its way into
AceHack and Nethack4.

With the former three it's a user configurable option, with NetHack4
OTOH it is not (makes me wonder how likely it is to hit the worst case
for the sorting algorithm used by qsort with pudding farming in nh4).

This actually fits my definition of being not a nuisance to the player
but of course it only reduces and doesn't prevent information leakage.

If you really wanted you'd have to go further and do something more
drastic in the bones generation code. For example replacing the
inventory items with others items of the same item class (this would
of course reduce the appeal of bones by a big factor as the bones
inventory wouldn't reflect a real inventory anymore) or - instead of
dropping all the items at the place of death - adding the items to the
inventories of the monster on the level.

